  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For open pipe&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℓ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>360</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p>For the closed at one end pipe, let the velocity of sound in gas at&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℓ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Since same tuning fork is used frequency will be same and thus,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>720</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p><p>Also&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>∝</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></msqrt><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>720</mn><mo>×</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>273</mn><mn>303</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>683</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>.</p>"
